## Flag → handler/level wiring detail (polish pass 6, §3 CLI)

Concrete construction in main.go (this bead owns the implementation; wa-jlb.5 owns the flag declaration):

```go
func makeLogger(verbose, quiet, jsonOut bool) *slog.Logger {
    level := slog.LevelInfo
    switch {
    case verbose && quiet:
        // already rejected at flag-parse time; defensive
        level = slog.LevelInfo
    case verbose:
        level = slog.LevelDebug
    case quiet:
        level = slog.LevelWarn
    }
    opts := &slog.HandlerOptions{Level: level}
    var h slog.Handler
    if jsonOut {
        h = slog.NewJSONHandler(os.Stderr, opts)
    } else {
        h = slog.NewTextHandler(os.Stderr, opts)
    }
    return slog.New(h)
}
```

slog output goes to **stderr** so subcommand stdout (sample-output lines, dry-run estimates, feed XML on `publish --dry-run`) stays parseable for piping.

## Test rows for flag-driven behavior

| Test name                      | Setup                | Expectation |
|--------------------------------|----------------------|-------------|
| default_level_is_info          | no flags             | INFO captured; DEBUG suppressed |
| verbose_enables_debug          | --verbose            | DEBUG line captured |
| quiet_suppresses_info          | --quiet              | INFO suppressed; WARN captured |
| json_emits_json_lines          | --json               | every log line is parseable JSON |
| json_plus_verbose              | --json --verbose     | JSON output includes DEBUG records |
| verbose_and_quiet_rejected     | --verbose --quiet    | exits non-zero with clear message |
| stdout_unaffected_by_log_level | --verbose            | stdout is unchanged (logs went to stderr) |
| no_secret_in_log_output        | inject token in URL  | log line shows redacted URL |

[pane-2] 408 classification realigned. retry.go and client.go now agree.

## Fix

`internal/tts/retry.go::classifyHTTPStatus` got an explicit case for 408 (Request Timeout) returning `retryVerdictRetryable` with computed backoff. Inserted between the 429 and 402/403 cases so the order — 200 → 429 → 408 → 402/403 → 5xx → 4xx-default → default — keeps the most-specific overrides above the range checks.

```go
case statusCode == http.StatusRequestTimeout:
    // 408 (Request Timeout) is retryable: the server told us it
    // gave up waiting, which on a fresh attempt with backoff
    // commonly succeeds. wa-wcu pinned this case explicitly so
    // classifyHTTPStatus and client.retryableStatusCode agree —
    // previously 408 fell through to the 4xx-default branch and
    // reported fatal, contradicting *APIError.Retryable=true on
    // the same status. Retry-After is not standard on 408, so
    // computed backoff is the only signal.
    return retryDecision{verdict: retryVerdictRetryable, sleep: computeBackoff(attempt, baseSeconds, rng)}
```

Comment cites the bead so future-me reading the case understands why 408 is broken out from the 4xx range.

## Tests

Two new test rows pin the verdict + the cross-function consistency invariant:

| name | what it covers |
|------|----------------|
| `TestClassifyHTTPResponse/http_408` | row added next to 429: 408 → retryable, sleep 2-3s (computed backoff with Retry-After absent) |
| `TestStatusClassificationConsistency` | new function: for each of {200, 400, 402, 403, 404, **408**, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504}, asserts `client.retryableStatusCode(code) == (classifyHTTPStatus(...).verdict == retryVerdictRetryable)`. 200 is the documented carve-out (one returns false, the other returns retryVerdictSuccess — both agree it isn't a retry candidate, which is the invariant). |

The consistency test is structural — adding a new code to `retryableStatusCode` without a matching arm in `classifyHTTPStatus` now fails CI with the exact code that diverged. Closes the door on the wa-wcu defect class, not just this one instance.

## Verification

- `go test -v -run 'TestClassifyHTTPResponse|TestStatusClassificationConsistency' ./internal/tts/` — 23 subtests pass (12 existing rows + 1 new 408 row + 11 consistency subtests).
- `go test ./...` — all 14 packages green; tts in 0.033s.
- `go vet ./...` clean.

## Coordination

- Reservations on `internal/tts/retry.go` and `internal/tts/retry_test.go` released after commit. Did not touch `internal/tts/client.go` (pane-5's wa-3gf territory) — the canonical answer (408 = retryable) was already in client.go; only retry.go was wrong.
- pane-5 working on wa-3gf: clean file separation. They edit client.go + build_pipeline.go, I edited retry.go + retry_test.go. If they ship first, my changes rebase cleanly.
